scmaps bundles atlas data from three sources (src/scmaps/data/). The MIT
licence in LICENSE covers the scmaps code only; each data file is
redistributed under the terms of its source.


1. FLAT.surf.gii, SUIT.shape.gii
   The SUIT cerebellar flatmap and its shading underlay, by the Diedrichsen
   lab (Western University).

   Source: SUITPy (https://github.com/DiedrichsenLab/SUITPy), under the MIT
   licence with an acknowledgement clause (LICENSES/SUITPy.txt).

   Please cite:
   - Diedrichsen J, Zotow E (2015). Surface-based display of volume-averaged
     cerebellar imaging data. PLoS ONE 10(7): e0133402.
     https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0133402
   - Diedrichsen J (2006). A spatially unbiased atlas template of the human
     cerebellum. NeuroImage 33(1): 127-138.
     https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2006.05.056
   - Wang Y, Li Y, Arafat B, Ashkanichenarlogh V, Nettekoven C, Pinho AL,
     Hernandez-Castillo CR, Marquand AF, Diedrichsen J (2026). SUITPy: a
     Python-based toolbox for the analysis of cerebellar functional and
     anatomical imaging data across the human lifespan. Imaging Neuroscience
     4, IMAG.a.1323. https://doi.org/10.1162/IMAG.a.1323


2. cerebellum_labels.npz
   The Nettekoven et al. (2024) asymmetric 32-region functional parcellation
   of the cerebellum (NettekovenAsym32), as one label per SUIT flatmap vertex,
   in the atlas's current numbering.

   Source: the Diedrichsen lab's cerebellar atlas collection
   (https://github.com/DiedrichsenLab/cerebellar_atlases,
   Nettekoven_2024/atl-NettekovenAsym32_dseg.label.gii; a copy is in
   tools/source/), under a Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) licence.

   Changes: none to the labels or names; stored as an integer array (.npz).

   Please cite:
   - Nettekoven C, Zhi D, Shahshahani L, Pinho AL, Saadon-Grosman N,
     Buckner RL, Diedrichsen J (2024). A hierarchical atlas of the human
     cerebellum for functional precision mapping. Nature Communications 15:
     8376. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-52371-w


3. subcortex_surfaces.npz
   Surfaces of the 32 ROIs of the Melbourne Subcortex Atlas, Scale II, 3T
   (MNI 2 mm), by Ye Tian and colleagues.

   Source: https://github.com/yetianmed/subcortex, under the Melbourne
   Subcortex Atlas License, which allows the atlas to be used, copied,
   modified, merged, published and distributed, on the condition that any
   publication that uses it cites the paper below.

   Changes: each ROI's voxels turned into a surface (MATLAB's
   boundary(..., 0.5)) and stored as .npz.

   Please cite:
   - Tian Y, Margulies DS, Breakspear M, Zalesky A (2020). Topographic
     organization of the human subcortex unveiled with functional
     connectivity gradients. Nature Neuroscience 23: 1421-1432.
     https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-020-00711-6
